course: dictionary
lesson: 7093
title: Peaceable and peaceably
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Peaceable is an adjective. It describes a person, place or meeting that does not want to fight, or that is calm and free from fighting. Add -ly and you get peaceably, an adverb, which tells you how something is done: calmly, without a fight.
explain: Read the clues around the word. «Isaiah foresaw a peaceable kingdom where the wolf lives with the lamb» tells you that in this kingdom a wolf, which would normally hunt a lamb, lives calmly beside it. So peaceable must mean peaceful and gentle, with no fighting.
explain: The sentence goes on: «swords are beaten into ploughshares, the blades of ploughs: weapons turned into tools for farming.» Swords are weapons, and here they become farming tools. That is another clue that peaceable means a world without war. To check, swap in peaceful. The sentence still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
fact: Peaceable means not wanting to fight or argue, and liking peace.
fact: Peaceable can also mean calm and without fighting, as in «a peaceable meeting».
fact: Peaceable is an adjective, and its adverb is peaceably, as in «settle peaceably».
fact: In religion lessons, the «peaceable kingdom» is Isaiah's picture of a world where the wolf lives with the lamb.
fact: Peaceful is a close synonym of peaceable, so it is a useful check when you read the word in a text.
exercise: «Isaiah foresaw a peaceable kingdom where the wolf lives with the lamb.» What is a peaceable kingdom? | A farm where the ploughs are broken | *A world where the wolf lives peacefully with the lamb | A kingdom full of wolves hunting lambs | A castle with swords on the walls
exercise: «The protesters marched peaceably, with no fighting.» What does peaceably mean here? | Quickly, while running | Hiding from everyone | Loudly and angrily | *Calmly and without violence
exercise: Copy the word from «swords are beaten into ploughshares» that names a weapon. | kingdom | ploughshares | *swords | farming
test: Which word is the adverb form of peaceable? | peace | *peaceably | peacemaker | peaceable
test: «The peaceable villagers welcomed the travellers.» What does peaceable suggest about the villagers? | *They are gentle and do not fight | They are hungry and cold | They hide from visitors | They are always at war
exam: Which sentence uses peaceable correctly? | The peaceable storm knocked over the trees | The peaceable soldiers started a loud fight | *The peaceable village welcomed the visitors with smiles | The dog was peaceable, so it chased every cat in the street
